        "section": "json",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "Unlike \"pickle\" and \"marshal\", JSON is not a framed protocol, so trying to serialize multiple objects with repeated calls to \"dump()\" using the same *fp* will result in an invalid JSON file.",
        "title": "json"
      },
      {
        "end": 318,
        "estimated_tokens": 92,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 0,
        "record_id": "18893306b3c2b47f6463001c",
        "score": 0.37260043715457497,
        "section": "pickle",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "* JSON, by default, can only represent a subset of the Python built-in types, and no custom classes; pickle can represent an extremely large number of Python types (many of them automatically, by clever usage of Python's introspection facilities; complex cases can be tackled by implementing specific object APIs);",
        "title": "pickle"
      },
      {
        "end": 820,
        "estimated_tokens": 85,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 3,
        "record_id": "18893306b3c2b47f6463001c",
        "score": 0.3538504371545749,
        "section": "pickle",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 533,
        "text": "The data format used by \"pickle\" is Python-specific. This has the advantage that there are no restrictions imposed by external standards such as JSON (which can't represent pointer sharing); however it means that non-Python programs may not be able to reconstruct pickled Python objects.",
        "title": "pickle"
      },
      {
        "end": 1301,
        "estimated_tokens": 47,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 3,
        "position": 5,
        "record_id": "859fda16a4d715b5f6c73141",
        "score": 0.34376380775296245,
        "section": "json",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 1160,
        "text": "Serialize *obj* as a JSON formatted stream to *fp* (a \".write()\"-supporting *file-like object*) using this Python-to-JSON conversion table.",
        "title": "json"
      },
      {
        "end": 1232,
        "estimated_tokens": 40,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 6,
        "record_id": "224d71d9f13fc0d43000d9c5",
        "score": 0.34248191386276366,
        "section": "pickle",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 1126,
        "text": "* JSON is interoperable and widely used outside of the Python ecosystem, while pickle is Python-specific;",
        "title": "pickle"
      },
      {
        "end": 435,
        "estimated_tokens": 42,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
